# Domain layer rules

- The Domain layer may only depend on `Core/src/Core`; do not add references to `Application`, `Persistence`, `Api`, or `Infrastructure`.
- Prefer straightforward assignments and simple control flow in entity methods. Do **not** use third-party **`Guard`** packs or throw **`DomainException`**. For preconditions, use **`Azoxia.Core.Extensions.GuardExtensions`** with **`ErrorCode`** values (**`AzoxiaErrorCodes`**, **`DomainErrorCodes`**) so failures are **`AzoxiaException`** — never **`ArgumentNullException`** / **`ArgumentException`**.
- Keep the domain model behavior-centric: business rules live in entities/aggregates; I/O stays in outer layers.
- **No static methods:** Do not declare **`static` methods** in the Domain layer (including private helpers on entities and value types). **Exception:** C# **`operator` members** (`implicit`, `explicit`, and other operators) must be `static` by language rules. Prefer **`private` instance methods** on the same type for shared logic; if logic is read-model-only or does not belong on the aggregate, move it to **Application**. **Allowed:** `DomainErrorCodes` as a **`public static` holder** of **`static readonly`** error values (no methods); **`const`** fields where appropriate. On entities, prefer **instance** fields over `static readonly` when representing per-instance configuration that is not a `const`.
- **Entities (`src/Domain/Entities/**`) — no public instance methods:** Do not declare **public instance methods** on entity classes. Stable external shape uses **properties** (including expression-bodied members), **constructors**, and EF navigation accessors; mutating or invariant-preserving behavior uses **`protected internal`** / **`internal`** methods as appropriate. Read-model projections that assemble value objects from stored scalar columns (for example mapping parallel amount/currency fields to `Money`) belong in **Application** (handlers or small mappers/extensions), not on the entity. **Value types**, **enums**, **`DomainErrorCodes`**, and similar non-entity types may keep **public** constructors, operators, and constants per existing patterns.
- Preserve `#region` order: `Fields > Ctors > Utils > Methods > Properties`.
- Under `#region Properties`, order sub-regions as `Scalar > Computed > Navigation > Collection`; within each group, order members alphabetically.
- Express nullability explicitly (`string?`, `Type?`); avoid unnecessary `!`.
- Use concise, meaningful XML summaries on every **public** type member and **`protected` / `protected internal` / `internal`** instance member where exposed outside the type, in a single language (English). Entity classes focus documentation on **properties** and non-public behavior methods (since **public instance methods** are not added on entities).
